WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:02.008
Pronouns.

00:00:02.008 --> 00:00:05.086
Trace the pronoun back to its noun, then make them match.

00:00:06.648 --> 00:00:08.398
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:08.398 --> 00:00:13.308
The choices are pronouns, like it, its, they, or their.

00:00:13.308 --> 00:00:16.648
And the noun they refer to is often far back in the sentence.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.039
It's testing whether the pronoun matches the noun it replaces.

00:00:22.102 --> 00:00:23.607
Here's the method.

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:25.692
Find the noun it replaces.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.562
Trace it back, even past commas.

00:00:28.562 --> 00:00:31.712
Count it: one, or more than one?

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.022
Organizations count as one.

00:00:34.022 --> 00:00:35.482
Pick the match.

00:00:35.482 --> 00:00:37.287
One takes it and its.

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:39.567
More than one takes they and their.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:43.000
Then check the form: its versus it's, who versus whom.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:48.636
Rule one: companies, teams, and museums are singular.

00:00:48.636 --> 00:00:51.391
The museum changed their hours is wrong.

00:00:51.391 --> 00:00:53.110
The museum changed its hours.

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:59.058
Rule two: its, with no apostrophe, means belonging to it.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.388
It's, with an apostrophe, means it is.

00:01:02.388 --> 00:01:05.132
So the town and its festival has no apostrophe.

00:01:06.206 --> 00:01:12.551
Rule three: after words like to, for, and with, use me, him, or them.

00:01:12.551 --> 00:01:14.341
Not to Priya and I.

00:01:14.341 --> 00:01:15.801
To Priya and me.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.854
Test it by dropping Priya: to me.

00:01:18.914 --> 00:01:20.419
Let's try one.

00:01:20.419 --> 00:01:23.929
First, skip the extra part between the commas.

00:01:23.929 --> 00:01:25.524
Who is celebrating?

00:01:25.524 --> 00:01:26.914
The orchestra.

00:01:26.914 --> 00:01:30.289
That's one group, so the pronoun must be singular.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:31.734
Their is plural.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:35.054
It's, with an apostrophe, means it is.

00:01:35.054 --> 00:01:36.684
They're means they are.

00:01:36.684 --> 00:01:41.812
Its, with no apostrophe, means belonging to the orchestra, so the answer is B.

00:01:42.873 --> 00:01:45.188
Watch out for the plural decoy.

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:48.603
Teachers sits right there, pulling you toward their.

00:01:48.603 --> 00:01:50.973
But the teachers aren't celebrating.

00:01:50.973 --> 00:01:52.062
The orchestra is.

00:01:53.114 --> 00:01:59.774
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the rules, and the trap.

00:01:59.774 --> 00:02:02.594
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
